<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obizzo II d'Este</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1247–1293</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Obizzo II d'Este was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> from 1264, when the citizens proclaimed him perpetual lord after the death of his grandfather Azzo VII. He also gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> in 1288 and Reggio in 1289, laying the foundations of the Este state that ruled these cities for centuries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> placed him among the tyrants in the Inferno.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obizzo-ii-deste.jpg" alt="Obizzo II d'Este" width="303" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obizzo_II_d%27Este3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
